{"id": "fs_166", "fact": "Virtual OS Museum — a QEMU-based Linux VM containing 1700+ pre-installed operating systems from 1948 (Manchester Baby) to present. 570+ distinct OSes across 250+ platforms including CTSS, Multics, Plan 9, BeOS, Windows 1.0 through Longhorn beta, PalmOS, Newton OS, IRIX, A/UX, NeXTSTEP, and dozens of obscure systems. Ships with a custom emulator-independent launcher with snapshot/rollback. Available in full (offline) and lite (on-demand download) editions. Represents years of dedication to preserving computing history. HN #3, 444pts, 101 comments, May 20 2026.", "source": "https://virtualosmuseum.org/ (HN #3, 444pts, May 20 2026)", "date": "2026-05-20", "tags": "persistent,computing-history,virtualization,preservation,open-source,retro", "confidence": 0.92}
{"id": "fs_167", "fact": "CLI-Anything ecosystem (HKUDS, 37.6k★, +1027/day May 20 2026) has grown to 60+ agent-native CLI tools registered on CLI-Hub, including LLDB debugger, Zotero, Firefly III, LibreOffice, Ink/Stitch embroidery, and more. Each tool ships as SKILL.md + CLI harness, installable via `npx skills add`. Community-contributed with CLA process, CI validation, and e2e tests. Philosophy: 'Today's Software Serves Humans. Tomorrow's Users will be Agents.' Signals maturation of the agent-native software paradigm.", "source": "https://clianything.cc/ + https://github.com/HKUDS/CLI-Anything (GitHub Trending #2, May 20 2026)", "date": "2026-05-20", "tags": "stable,agents,CLI,automation,ecosystem,software-architecture,open-source", "confidence": 0.91}
{"id": "fs_168", "fact": "Andrej Karpathy joined Anthropic (announced May 19-20, 2026). HN #1 with 990 points and 394 comments — the largest story on Hacker News that day. Career trajectory: OpenAI founding member → Tesla AI Director → Eureka Labs (AI education startup) → Anthropic. Signals continued concentration of top AI talent in frontier labs. Community discussion focused on implications for AI safety direction and Anthropic's strategic positioning.", "source": "https://news.ycombinator.com/ (HN #1, 990pts, May 20 2026) / https://twitter.com/karpathy", "date": "2026-05-20", "tags": "timely,AI,industry,talent,Anthropic,people", "confidence": 0.93}
{"id": "fs_169", "fact": "Growing Neural Cellular Automata (Distill.pub, Mordvintsev et al. 2020) — a neural network trained as a cellular automaton that grows complex, self-repairing patterns from a single seed cell. Each cell only knows its neighbors' states (no global control), requires ~10KB ROM + 256B RAM per cell. Demonstrates that decentralized local rules can produce coherent global structures that regenerate after damage. The paper speculates this approach could be used for designing reliable, self-organizing agents — directly relevant to the philosophical design of autonomous AI agents.", "source": "https://distill.pub/2020/growing-ca/", "date": "2026-05-20", "tags": "stable,AI,self-organization,cellular-automata,neural-networks,emergence", "confidence": 0.91}
{"id": "fs_170", "fact": "Google's Gemini 3.5 Flash launched (May 20, 2026) — positioned as 'faster, cheaper, smart-enough' inference model. HN #1 with 468pts/367 comments. Reflects industry stratification: flagship models for deep reasoning, Flash-class for high-frequency low-cost daily tasks.", "source": "https://blog.google/ (HN #1, 468pts, May 20 2026)", "date": "2026-05-20", "tags": "timely,AI,Google,models,industry-trends", "confidence": 0.9}
{"id": "fs_171", "fact": "Apple announced new accessibility features (May 20, 2026) — HN #9 with 561pts/286 comments. In contrast to Google's Search UI redesign dominating the same day's front page with negative sentiment, Apple's accessibility features generated overwhelmingly positive user responses. Highlights how 'what you build' (features for the few) can generate more genuine goodwill than 'what you change' (UI for everyone).", "source": "https://news.ycombinator.com/ (Apple accessibility #9, 561pts, May 20 2026) / apple.com", "date": "2026-05-20", "tags": "timely,Apple,accessibility,design,tech-industry", "confidence": 0.88}
{"id": "fs_173", "fact": "SpiderMonkey 在 Firefox 148 默认关闭 asm.js 优化并计划移除代码，标志着 Web 平台从 'JavaScript 子集提速' 过渡到 'WebAssembly 原生管线' 的历史拐点。asm.js 的长期价值不在继续维护，而在它证明了 Web 可承载近原生性能，从而催化了 WebAssembly 的诞生与普及。", "source": "https://spidermonkey.dev/blog/2026/05/20/saying-goodbye-to-asmjs.html", "date": "2026-05-21", "tags": "stable,timely,web,wasm,javascript,compiler-history", "confidence": 0.9}
